  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responding to Trafficking in Persons for Forced Criminality in Myanmar - Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective is to contribute to strengthened and more effective measures combatting transnational organized crime, including cybercrime and trafficking for forced criminality, in Myanmar. The project will also employ a victim-centered approach, providing essential trauma-informed services, safe spaces, and direct support to survivors, ensuring their mental well-being and reducing their risk of re-trafficking. The project involves information gathering, collaboration with key stakeholders, and training programs that equip embassies, law enforcement, and organizations with the necessary tools to combat trafficking more effectively.</narrative>
  </description>
